  "description": "CIPJOC crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group F -4 3 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H128 Cu8 Gd4 N8 O32 2+,2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu7 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu8 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.212-3.985 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.74-111.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C94H173Cu8Gd4N13O57. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III), Cu(II).",
